{
  "slug": "artist:ll-cool-j",
  "name": "LL Cool J",
  "editorial_article": "James Todd Smith, known professionally as LL Cool J, is a Queens-born rapper who debuted in 1987 on the Def Jam and Columbia labels. His prolific career spans over 14 studio albums, including the 2024 release The Force, which features production rooted in boom bap and jazzy hip-hop aesthetics. Throughout his tenure, he has collaborated with artists ranging from Jennifer Lopez on the 2002 chart-topping single All I Have to Brad Paisley on the 2013 track Accidental Racist. His discography highlights include influential records like 1990's Mama Said Knock You Out, with music videos frequently directed by Hype Williams and Paris Barclay. Across his career, he has appeared on numerous soundtracks and joint projects, contributing to compilations such as the Violator albums and participating in high-profile collective efforts like the 2010 charity single We Are the World 25 for Haiti.",
